      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two hundred and seventy seven patients with coronary heart disease, including 182 with postinfarction cardiosclerosis underwent 24-hour Holter monitoring. A significant correlation was found between the number of coupled ventricular arrhythmias, ventricular tachycardia paroxysms and development of congestive heart failure in patients with postinfarct cardiosclerosis. With evolving metabolic deficiency as evidenced by thallium-201 myocardial scintigraphy, the incidence of congestive heart failure and ventricular arrhythmias increased among the patients."},
